cdp:eu-EMFAF-2026-PIA-ARCTIC cdp:fromSource cdp:euportalSource;
    xyz:title "Support to awareness raising about the Arctic communities, including Indigenous People";
    xyz:description "Objective: The Arctic is undergoing rapid environmental and geopolitical change, with increasing impacts on its inhabitants, particularly Indigenous Peoples. As external interest in the region grows, ensuring their meaningful involvement in policymaking processes that affect them is essential.";
    xyz:url "https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/EMFAF-2026-PIA-ARCTIC";
    xyz:deadlineModel "single_stage";
    xyz:deadline "2026-08-20"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date>;
    xyz:status "ended".
cdp:eu-EMFAF-2026-PIA-MSP cdp:fromSource cdp:euportalSource;
    xyz:title "Projects to Support Maritime Spatial Planning (MSP)";
    xyz:description "Expected Impact: Proposals are expected to ensure that maritime plans are coherent and coordinated across the marine region concerned. Applicants should identify in their proposals the specific expected impacts in relation to the targeted priorities of the call, as set out in the call document. Objective: The objective of this call for proposals is to facilitate the implementation of Maritime Spatial Planning in the EU, including through the effective application of Directive 2014/89 establishing a framework for MSP. This call is intended to fund projects to develop innovative responses to tackle specific challenges that EU Members States might encounter when putting into effect, monitoring and/or revising their maritime spatial plans. Many of these challenges are common to coastal Member States. There is thus a shared interest in developing innovative responses that can apply within a sea basin and/or across sea basins. The specific scope and themes are described in the call document. Scope: This call is intended to fund projects to develop innovative responses to tackle specific challenges that EU Members States might encounter when putting into effect, monitoring and/or revising their maritime spatial plans. Many of these challenges are common to coastal Member States. There is thus a shared interest in developing innovative responses that can apply within a sea basin and/or across sea basins. The specific scope and themes are described in the call document.";
    xyz:url "https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/EMFAF-2026-PIA-MSP";
    xyz:deadlineModel "single_stage";
    xyz:deadline "2026-04-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date>;
    xyz:status "ended".
cdp:eu-EP-COMM-SUBV-2026-EYE-VILLAGE cdp:fromSource cdp:euportalSource;
    xyz:title "EYE 2027 - ORGANISATION OF THE PROGRAMME OF THE EYE VILLAGE";
    xyz:url "https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-details/EP-COMM-SUBV-2026-EYE-VILLAGE";
